# steps/table-receiver.md §10: two parts (harness Parts) each declare k at its root -- two Structures of the
# program with no name, one per part -- and the source declares its own k, 1.  nodeA reads its part's root's k
# explicitly, 5, nodeB its own, 8, and the source's code its own, 1.  peekA and peekB read k bare: a hidden
# input, which the caller binds first (book §12: the caller's local binding, then its inherited input, then the
# callee's lexical lookup) -- the source's k is a field its code uses, so both read 1.  Entry 7.
size_t: k 1U
size_t: a 0U
size_t: b 0U
size_t: na 0U
size_t: nb 0U
a: peekA()
b: peekB()
na: nodeA()
nb: nodeB()
if: na != 5U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: nb != 8U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 82; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: k != 1U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: a != 1U || b != 1U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 84; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
